    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1368">

                <pb facs="1342" n="1332" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1332"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/9–1949: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">McConaughy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-09-09T19:00:00+08:00">September 9,
                            1949—7 p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 9—10:02 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3759. Dept will have noted Downs’ message for Buckley, APL, commenting on
                    Nationalists’ conditions re entry <hi rendition="#italic">Gordon</hi> (ConGentel
                    3718, September 8, repeated Nanking 1942; Canton 1091). Consulate General
                    considers Downs’ telegram comprehensive and fair-minded statement of case
                    against supine acceptance extreme Nationalist demand on <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gordon</hi>.</p>
                <p>Consulate General believes strong representation should be made to Nationalist
                    Govt pointing out entry of <hi rendition="#italic">Gordon</hi> Shanghai should
                    be permitted without interference along those lines indicated ourtel 3700, <pb
                        facs="1343" n="1333" xml:id="pg1333"/> September 7; repeated Nanking 1934;
                    Canton 1086. In view Dept’s statement re illegality blockade, unless declared
                    and effectively maintained, voluntary submission large American liner to search
                    would be interpreted here as acceptance or at least toleration blockade. Suggest
                    certification procedure recommended reftel should be satisfactory evidence
                    ship’s crew, passengers and cargo are as represented, and there should be no
                    reason for interference with entry and exit vessel.</p>
                <p>Submission to humiliating procedure prescribed by Nationalists would seem
                    warranted only if Dept considers no other way of assuring entry ship.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 3760 [<hi rendition="#italic">3759</hi>]; repeated Nanking 1963;
                    OffEmb Canton 1100.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">McConaughy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
